1. Basic Data types:
  
	int - integer

    	Stores whole numbers without decimal points.

	float - Decimal number

	    stores floating point numbers with limited precision.

	double - Higher-presicion decimal numers

	    Usually provides more precision than a float

	char - Character

    	Stores a single character, represented by an integer value in C.

	_Bool - Boolean value

    	Stores either 0 (flase) or 1 (true)
